WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.134 --> 00:00:17.999
The children were drinking tea with Mr. Perks in the porter's room at the station.

2
00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:21.557
They had brought their own cups and some biscuits.

3
00:00:21.558 --> 00:00:28.497
Perks made tea in a beer can as usual, and everyone was happy and talkative.

4
00:00:28.498 --> 00:00:32.324
"When is your birthday, Mr. Perks?" Bobbie asked him.

5
00:00:32.325 --> 00:00:35.339
"My birthday?" asked Perks.

6
00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:39.107
"I gave up birthdays before you were born!"

7
00:00:39.108 --> 00:00:44.401
"But you must have been born at some time," said Phyllis thoughtfully.

8
00:00:44.402 --> 00:00:50.658
"Even if it was twenty years ago—or sixty or seventy!"

9
00:00:50.659 --> 00:00:55.035
"Not that long ago, missy!" Perks grinned as he answered.

10
00:00:55.036 --> 00:00:59.802
"Actually, I'll be 32 on the fifteenth of this month."

11
00:00:59.803 --> 00:01:02.158
Later the children talked.

12
00:01:02.159 --> 00:01:04.934
Perks was the best friend they had made.

13
00:01:04.935 --> 00:01:10.427
So they decided to do something special for his birthday.

14
00:01:10.428 --> 00:01:15.619
The next day at breakfast Mother smiled as she gave the children porridge and milk.

15
00:01:15.620 --> 00:01:21.141
"I've sold another story," she said, "so there'll be buns for tea."

16
00:01:21.142 --> 00:01:24.314
Phyllis, Bobbie, and Peter looked at each other.

17
00:01:24.315 --> 00:01:27.362
They were thinking the same thing.

18
00:01:27.363 --> 00:01:32.299
"Mother, can we have buns on the fifteenth instead?" Bobbie asked.

19
00:01:32.300 --> 00:01:36.475
"It's Perks' birthday, and we thought we'd have a small party."

20
00:01:36.476 --> 00:01:39.774
"Yes, you can," Mother replied.

21
00:01:39.775 --> 00:01:42.886
"We'll put his name on the buns with icing!"

22
00:01:42.887 --> 00:01:45.919
The children looked excited.

23
00:01:45.920 --> 00:01:49.917
Later Bobbie said, "I think we need flowers as well."

24
00:01:49.918 --> 00:01:53.530
"Yes, we need more ideas!

25
00:01:53.531 --> 00:01:57.683
Let's all be quiet and think," said Phyllis.

26
00:01:57.684 --> 00:02:01.079
"Hooray!" Peter cried suddenly.

27
00:02:01.080 --> 00:02:04.172
"I've got it!" He jumped up.

28
00:02:04.173 --> 00:02:08.057
"What?" said his sisters eagerly.

29
00:02:08.058 --> 00:02:11.753
"Well, Perks is so nice to everybody.

30
00:02:11.754 --> 00:02:16.614
There must be lots of people in the village who'd like to give presents to Perks.

31
00:02:16.615 --> 00:02:19.483
Let's go round and ask everyone."

32
00:02:19.484 --> 00:02:24.823
"Mother said we shouldn't ask people for things," said Bobbie doubtfully.

33
00:02:24.824 --> 00:02:29.580
"For ourselves, silly, not for other people," said Peter.

34
00:02:29.581 --> 00:02:35.274
So they went. The old lady at the post office didn't want to give Perks a present.

35
00:02:35.275 --> 00:02:40.561
"It's my birthday tomorrow and nobody cares about it," she said.

36
00:02:40.562 --> 00:02:44.717
"Why should I care about Perks' birthday?"

37
00:02:44.718 --> 00:02:47.599
The children left and went elsewhere.

38
00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:50.946
Some people were kind and some were not.

39
00:02:50.947 --> 00:02:55.344
At the end of the day, Peter wrote a list of things they'd received.

40
00:02:55.345 --> 00:02:59.733
He wrote it in the book where he kept the numbers of train engines.

41
00:02:59.734 --> 00:03:00.946
Presents Given:

42
00:03:00.947 --> 00:03:03.181
a pipe from the sweet shop

43
00:03:03.182 --> 00:03:05.753
some tea from the village store

44
00:03:05.754 --> 00:03:07.159
Presents Promised:

45
00:03:07.160 --> 00:03:09.414
some meat from the butcher

46
00:03:09.415 --> 00:03:11.853
six eggs from the farmer

47
00:03:11.854 --> 00:03:14.991
a spade from the blacksmith

48
00:03:14.992 --> 00:03:18.397
Early the next morning, Bobbie woke Phyllis.

49
00:03:18.398 --> 00:03:21.848
They had a plan but had not told Peter.

50
00:03:21.849 --> 00:03:24.080
He would think it was silly.

51
00:03:24.081 --> 00:03:26.905
They cut a bunch of roses and wrote a card:

52
00:03:26.906 --> 00:03:31.646
"For Mrs. Ransome, Happy Birthday."

53
00:03:31.647 --> 00:03:35.672
Bobbie and Phyllis took the roses and card to the post office.

54
00:03:35.673 --> 00:03:39.794
They put them on the counter before the old lady came in.

55
00:03:39.795 --> 00:03:45.536
When they got home, Peter was telling Mother about their plan to give Perks gifts for his birthday.

56
00:03:45.537 --> 00:03:50.173
"It depends on how you give him the presents," Mother said.

57
00:03:50.174 --> 00:03:54.130
"I hope he won't be offended and think it's charity.

58
00:03:54.131 --> 00:03:57.119
Poor people are very proud, you know."

59
00:03:57.120 --> 00:04:01.011
"It isn't because he's poor," said Phyllis.

60
00:04:01.012 --> 00:04:05.175
"It's because we like him very much."

61
00:04:05.176 --> 00:04:11.571
The morning of the fifteenth, the children watched Mother decorate the buns with pink icing.

62
00:04:11.572 --> 00:04:17.066
Then they went to the village to collect the spade and eggs and other things people had promised.

63
00:04:17.067 --> 00:04:20.955
They passed the old lady at the post office.

64
00:04:20.956 --> 00:04:24.285
"Thank you for the roses," she said.

65
00:04:24.286 --> 00:04:28.619
"Here, take these for Perks' birthday present."

66
00:04:28.620 --> 00:04:32.296
She brought out a basket full of red gooseberries.

67
00:04:32.297 --> 00:04:34.677
"And wait one more moment.

68
00:04:34.678 --> 00:04:37.737
I have something else for Perks!"

69
00:04:37.738 --> 00:04:39.858
The children smiled.

70
00:04:39.859 --> 00:04:46.512
Perks was going to have the best birthday ever!
